# ── image-size 1.2.1 DoS (HIGH ×2) — no fixed release exists at all ──────────
# CVE-2025-71329 (crafted image buffer with zero-valued size) and CVE-2025-71330
# (crafted ICNS buffer). Trivy reports NO fixed version for either — 1.2.1 is
# the last release of the 1.x line (published 2025-04-02, the same day upstream
# moved on to 2.0.2), and 2.x is not marked fixed either, so bumping resolves
# nothing.
#
# Reachability: mobile/package-lock.json only, and only via metro — the Expo /
# React-Native DEV bundler (metro 0.83.x under @expo/metro and
# @react-native/community-cli-plugin). metro reads image dimensions while
# building the JS bundle on a developer machine or a CI runner; it does not ship
# in the compiled APK/IPA and does not run on any server. The images it reads
# are the repo's own committed assets, not untrusted input.
#
# Remove this entry when upstream publishes a fixed image-size that metro picks
# up. (added 2026-08-08)
# 2026-08-28: STILL VALID and still the ONLY genuinely unfixable npm entry left.
# GitHub Advisory Database still records the affected range as <= 2.0.2 with
# first_patched_version NONE for both CVEs, and mobile/package-lock.json still
# resolves image-size to 1.2.1 (single instance, node_modules/image-size).
CVE-2025-71329
CVE-2025-71330

